/51126"} "Betsy Mitchell"] ", who won the Trials, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/50953"} "Theresa Andrews"] ", who had not been expected to make the team. The Olympic final was led out by Dutchwoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/49319"} "Jolanda de Rover"] ", who was caught at the turn by Romanian " [:a {:href "/athletes/49926"} "Carmen Bunaciu"] ". At 75 metres, Bunaciu had fallen back as the two Americans gained on de Rover. The three touched almost together with Andrews winning gold in 1:02.55, followed by Mitchell in 1:02.63, and de Rover for the bronze in 1:02.91. At the Friendship Games, 24 days later, East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/47487"} "Ina Kleber"] " finally broke Reinisch’s world record, finishing in 1:00.59, a mark that would stand until 1991."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "242"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50953"} "Theresa Andrews"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:02.94 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:02.55 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "253"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51126"} "Betsy Mitchell"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:02.53 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:02.63 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "135"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/49319"} "Jolanda de Rover"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED